<code>assert 0 <= index && index < \old(this.size()) => (\old(this.get(index)) == null && this.get(index) == obj) || this.get(index) == obj;</code>

This assert statement reflects the condition that if the index is within the bounds of the initial size of the vector, then either the element at that index was initially null and is now set to the new object, or the element at that index is now set to the new object.
